You are continuing development on PitchIQ, an existing soccer-video tracking web application. Do not restart the project from scratch. First understand the existing architecture and preserve the working functionality described below.

PROJECT OVERVIEW

PitchIQ is a React/TypeScript/Vinext web application for labeling soccer players and tracking them through uploaded MP4 footage.

The intended workflow is:

1. Upload a soccer video.
2. Pause on a useful starting frame.
3. Detect or manually label the visible players and ball.
4. Assign players to Team A or Team B and connect boxes to roster identities.
5. Run automatic tracking.
6. Review uncertain observations and correct them manually.
7. Eventually generate soccer analytics such as formations, movement, ball progression, tactical events, player actions, and match reports.

The current version is V6. It is still an experimental tracking prototype, not a finished full-match analytics system.

